# kestrel's command line at boot (systemd EnvironmentFile). After editing:
#     sudo systemctl restart kestrel
#
# DRY-RUN AS SHIPPED: perception, modes, the script and the OSD line all run,
# and the would-be commands are computed -- but nothing is sent to the FC.
# The OSD says DRY. Add --allow-control only when the bench checklist in
# docs/pi5-ardupilot-setup.md has passed; the OSD then says LIVE.
#
# Even LIVE, ArduPilot's own mode gates it: commands go only in GUIDED,
# GUIDED_NOGPS, ALT_HOLD, LOITER and POSHOLD, and the mode wheel's FLY band
# sends nothing at all.
#
# /dev/ttyAMA0 is the Pi 5's GPIO 14/15 UART (dtparam=uart0=on; install_pi5.sh
# --enable-uart sets it). The ArduPilot port it is wired to needs
# SERIALn_PROTOCOL = 2 and SERIALn_BAUD = 115.

KESTREL_ARGS="--fc=mavlink --fc-port=/dev/ttyAMA0 --fc-baud=115200 --camera=0 --blackbox=/var/lib/kestrel/blackbox.bin"
